From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:23:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Return the picture buffers when their queue
 stops

Stopping the picture queue left its queued buffers with the driver, and
videobuf2 warned of a driver bug for each.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
index 2f5d5d950..4fa89f591 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
@@ -624,8 +624,10 @@ static void cedrus_context_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *queue)
 	v4l2_m2m_update_stop_streaming_state(ctx->v4l2.fh.m2m_ctx, queue);
 
 	/* Only stop the engine from the coded queue. */
-	if (format_type != CEDRUS_FORMAT_TYPE_CODED)
+	if (format_type != CEDRUS_FORMAT_TYPE_CODED) {
+		cedrus_context_queue_cleanup(queue, true);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	cedrus_engine_cleanup(ctx);
 
-- 
2.47.3

